    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27555" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maena</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mēna</span></b> ), ae, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαίνη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a kind of small sea-fish</i>, eaten
			salted by the poor, <i><span class="en">Plin. 32, 11, 53, § 149</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Ov. Hal.
				120</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 11, 31, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12, 32, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pers. 3,
			76</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acipenserem maenae non anteponere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 2, 28, 91</span></i>
			.—As a term of reproach: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deglupta maena,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 5, 5, 33</span></i>
			.</div>
